  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Australia Skills Platform (PASP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Australia Skills Platform (PASP) seeks to equip a greater number of Pacific and Timor-Leste students and workers with the knowledge and skills to gain employment. PASP will form genuine partnerships in Pacific island countries and Timor-Leste to strengthen skills systems, be more responsive to national and regional labour market priorities, and improve access and participation. PASP is guided by the priorities of gender equality, disability equity and rights, and social inclusion (GEDSI), climate change resilience and locally led development principles.</narrative>
  </description>
